{
  "$comment": "Third-party skill directories vendored into plugins/nt-vendor/skills/. `path` is a directory, copied whole. `sha` and `files` are written by `node scripts/vendor-skills.mjs pull`; do not hand-edit them. To add a skill, append name/repo/ref/path/license and run `pull <name>` - naming it keeps other skills' upstream drift out of the same PR. `copyright` is written too, but only when absent: set it by hand for a license that names no holder, such as Apache-2.0.",
  "$dest": "A source vendored as material rather than as a skill of its own sets `dest` to the first-party skill directory that reads it, and `as` to the entry point's filename there. Skill discovery only walks plugins/<plugin>/skills/<name>/, and `as` moving the entry off SKILL.md means the tree cannot register however deep discovery goes. The prose ships without buying a listing entry, and one copy stays under `pull` and `verify`.",
  "$exclude": "Dropped from every copy: other-harness config, and anything that could be mistaken for our own repo wiring. Everything else comes across, because these skills link to their siblings.",
